{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-table"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"vue\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exports","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-table"},{"type":"text","value":" re-exports all of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/table-core"},{"type":"text","value":"'s APIs and the following:"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"usevuetable","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useVueTable"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Takes an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" object and returns a table."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n// ...render your table\n","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Vue component for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n<template>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr v-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n        <FlexRender\n          :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\"\n          :props=\"cell.getContext()\"\n        />\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</template>","lang":"vue"}],"headings":[{"id":"exports","text":"Exports","level":2},{"id":"usevuetable","text":"useVueTable","level":3},{"id":"flexrender","text":"FlexRender","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"vue\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/vue-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `useVueTable`\n\nTakes an `options` object and returns a table.\n\n```ts\nimport { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n// ...render your table\n\n```\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nA Vue component for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nExample:\n\n```vue\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n<template>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr v-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n        <FlexRender\n          :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\"\n          :props=\"cell.getContext()\"\n        />\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</template>\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Vue Table\n---\n\nThe `@tanstack/vue-table` adapter is a wrapper around the core table logic. Most of it's job is related to managing state the \"vue\" way, providing types and the rendering implementation of cell/header/footer templates.\n\n## Exports\n\n`@tanstack/vue-table` re-exports all of `@tanstack/table-core`'s APIs and the following:\n\n### `useVueTable`\n\nTakes an `options` object and returns a table.\n\n```ts\nimport { useVueTable } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\nconst table = useVueTable(options)\n// ...render your table\n\n```\n\n### `FlexRender`\n\nA Vue component for rendering cell/header/footer templates with dynamic values.\n\nExample:\n\n```vue\nimport { FlexRender } from '@tanstack/vue-table'\n\n<template>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr v-for=\"row in table.getRowModel().rows\" :key=\"row.id\">\n      <td v-for=\"cell in row.getVisibleCells()\" :key=\"cell.id\">\n        <FlexRender\n          :render=\"cell.column.columnDef.cell\"\n          :props=\"cell.getContext()\"\n        />\n      </td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</template>\n```\n"}
